---
// The side marker for a case-study header: which half of the practice this project sat on,
// and — since chooser andrewshiau-panel-marks Q5/06 — the way back to the index.
//
// The panel head used to open with the logo and then this line, so the figure was drawn
// TWICE, stacked, ~30px apart, at two sizes. The logo was there to be the link home; this
// line was there to name the side. One of them had to go, and the marker is the one that
// carries a fact, so it took the link as well.
//
// It draws `MarkFigure` side-aware: the whole figure where the page sat on both halves of the
// practice, the ring alone for design, the disc alone for build. A pairing is only drawn where
// there is one — the diagonal's whole subject is two things joined, and on `/work/luthier/`
// there is no second thing for the rule to reach.
//
// SAME GLYPH AS THE INDEX ROW NOW, at 26px instead of 18. The index used to draw a flat 22×8
// version, so this file's note read "the logo's figure, not the flat glyph the index uses";
// that glyph is gone (chooser: andrewshiau-mark-options, Q3/05 — see SideDot.astro). The two
// wrappers now differ only in size, hover and whether the word shows, which is what they should
// have differed in all along. It is not SideDot itself because that one clips its word and is
// not a link; both read their side from the same `sideOf`, so the fact can't drift.
//
// The WORD stays here, visible. The index hides it now (Q1/05) because eight rows repeating
// "Design + Build" was the loudest thing in that column; a panel head prints one marker, so the
// word costs nothing. It is no longer the ONLY non-colour signal — the ring/disc pair carries
// into greyscale where the two hues could not (navy and olive are 2.14:1 apart — STYLE.md) —
// but a shape a reader has to learn is not a label, so the word is not up for deletion.
import { sideOf, SIDE_LABEL } from '../data/experiments';
import MarkFigure from './MarkFigure.astro';
interface Props { href: string }
const { href } = Astro.props;
const side = sideOf(href);
---
<p class="smark">
  <a class="smark-home" href="/" aria-label="andrewshiau — home"
    ><MarkFigure side={side} />{SIDE_LABEL[side]}</a
  >
</p>
